---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="TCPendant | Projects | Wretzelectronics">
  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="detail-header">
      <h1 class="project-title">TCPendant</h1>
      <p class="project-tagline">
        A compact aluminum thermal pendant powered by an ESP32, custom high-current PCB driver stage, and a React Native mobile control app via BLE.
      </p>

      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag-badge">ESP32</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">Bluetooth LE</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">Custom PCB</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">Power Electronics</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">React Native</span>
      </div>

      <div class="action-row">
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/wretzel01/TCPendant" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer" 
          class="cyber-button"
        >
          <svg class="github-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18">
            <path fill="currentColor" d="M12 0C5.37 0 0 5.37 0 12c0 5.31 3.435 9.795 8.205 11.385.6.105.825-.255.825-.57 0-.285-.015-1.23-.015-2.235-3.015.555-3.795-.735-4.035-1.41-.135-.345-.72-1.41-1.23-1.695-.42-.225-1.02-.78-.015-.795.945-.015 1.62.87 1.845 1.23 1.08 1.815 2.805 1.305 3.495.99.105-.78.42-1.305.765-1.605-2.67-.3-5.46-1.335-5.46-5.925 0-1.305.465-2.385 1.23-3.225-.12-.3-.54-1.53.12-3.18 0 0 1.005-.315 3.3 1.23.96-.27 1.98-.405 3-.405s2.04.135 3 .405c2.295-1.56 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.65.24 2.88.12 3.18.765.84 1.23 1.905 1.23 3.225 0 4.605-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.925.435.375.81 1.095.81 2.22 0 1.605-.015 2.895-.015 3.3 0 .315.225.69.825.57A12.02 12.02 0 0024 12c0-6.63-5.37-12-12-12z"/>
          </svg>
          <span>View Source on GitHub</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="hero-image-wrapper">
      <img src="/images/projects/tcpendant.png" alt="TCPendant illuminated" class="detail-hero-img" />
    </div>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>System Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Thermal Core Pendant (TCPendant) is an embedded hardware project integrating precision thermal regulation, custom power switching electronics, and mobile connectivity within a hand-machined aluminum enclosure.
      </p>
      <p>
        The system bridges high-power switching (heating elements and addressable/PWM LED arrays) with low-power wireless control. An onboard ESP32 runs custom C++ firmware managing real-time PWM output, thermal sensing feedback, and GATT BLE server tasks, while a companion mobile application handles remote control and status telemetry.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Hardware Architecture & Power Electronics</h2>
      <p>
        The physical build evolved from a rapid perfboard proof-of-concept into a surface-mount custom PCB configured to drop directly into the machined aluminum body:
      </p>
      
      <div class="tech-spec-grid">
        <div class="spec-card">
          <h3>Thermal & Enclosure Design</h3>
          <p>
            The aluminum casing serves dual roles as a protective aesthetic shell and a primary heatsink/thermal dissipation surface. Mechanical clearances were kept under 0.5mm tolerances to maximize direct conductive contact with internal heating elements while isolating sensitive logic ICs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <h3>MOSFET Switching & Gate Drive</h3>
          <p>
            Thermal regulation is handled via low-side N-channel power MOSFET switching. Tuning the gate drive circuit was critical—mitigating gate capacitance issues (Q<sub>g</sub>) to ensure fast rise/fall times directly from 3.3V logic levels without dropping the FET into its linear region, keeping R<sub>DS(on)</sub> losses and thermal runaway to a minimum.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="photo-grid">
        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>Scale & Form Factor</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Machined aluminum body relative to scale and internal optic profile.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/tcpendant-scale.jpg" alt="TCPendant scale photo" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>Custom PCB Layout</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Integrated low-side MOSFET drivers, LED regulation, and power pathing.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/tcpendant-pcb.jpg" alt="TCPendant PCB front" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>Perfboard Validation</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Initial breadboard and perfboard stage verifying BLE stack and driver logic.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/tcpendant-perf-front.jpg" alt="TCPendant perfboard prototype" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Firmware & BLE Protocol</h2>
      <p>
        The ESP32 firmware manages non-blocking execution loops to maintain steady BLE responsiveness while driving high-frequency PWM channels:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Custom BLE GATT Server:</strong> Exposes dedicated service UUIDs for realtime control. Handles atomic write commands for brightness, animation modes, and duty cycles.</li>
        <li><strong>Thermal Safety Safeguards:</strong> Embedded safety limits and duty-cycle throttling prevent thermal overload when operating in enclosed pockets.</li>
        <li><strong>Lighting Engine:</strong> Low-latency transition calculations between discrete color modes and dynamic ambient animations.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Mobile App Interface (TCPendantApp)</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <strong>React Native</strong>, the mobile application provides direct, full-duplex communication with the pendant over BLE:
      </p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><code>ConnectionBanner</code>: Monitors RSSI, handles automatic reconnection logic, and displays live connection states.</li>
        <li><code>LEDBrightnessControls</code>: Real-time slider and preset input mapped to 8-bit / 10-bit hardware PWM resolution.</li>
        <li><code>LEDAnimationControls</code>: Mode switches driving pattern generators on the local hardware.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="diagram-block app-block">
        <h3>React Native Interface</h3>
        <p class="diagram-caption">Custom React Native UI showing ConnectionBanner state, animation modes, and LED control sliders.</p>
        <img src="/images/projects/tcpendant-app.jpg" alt="TCPendant mobile app screenshot" class="diagram-img app-img" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Engineering Challenges & Lessons Learned</h2>
      <div class="timeline-bullets">
        <p>
          <strong>FET Thermal Management:</strong> Early revisions suffered from high switching losses when driving low-threshold MOSFET gates directly from 3.3V microcontrollers without proper gate pull-down resistors and driver stages. Correcting gate switching speed drastically reduced idle heat.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Enclosure Isolation:</strong> Machining aluminum required exact component height planning. Thermally coupling the heat element to the chassis while keeping high-frequency microcontrollers isolated required strategic placement of thermal pads and ground planes on the PCB.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>BLE State Synchronization:</strong> Handled cross-platform BLE packet drop issues by implementing state acknowledgment and throttle-debouncing in React Native before pushing rapid slider updates to the hardware.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Current Revision &amp; Roadmap</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>v1 Status:</strong> Fully functional hardware housed in aluminum casing with stable BLE connectivity, custom React Native app control, and working LED lighting modes.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>v2 Planned:</strong> Redesigning the main PCB to incorporate inline current sensing (INA series IC) for closed-loop power monitoring, upgrading to an active PID thermal control loop, and refining the enclosure milling process for tighter seam sealing.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  /* Header Action Bar & GitHub Button */
  .action-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .cyber-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #ffffff;
    background: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-neon, #00f0ff);
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);
  }

  .cyber-button:hover {
    background: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.2);
    box-shadow: 0 0 18px var(--border-glow, rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.6));
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    color: var(--border-neon, #00f0ff);
  }

  .github-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    fill: currentColor; /* Ensures the SVG matches text color changes on hover */
  }

  .project-detail {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .detail-header {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .project-tagline {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tag-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .hero-image-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.2);
    background: #000;
  }

  .detail-hero-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 480px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .content-section p {
    color: var(--text-main, #e2e8f0);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .photo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .diagram-block {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .diagram-block h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--border-neon, #00f0ff);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .diagram-caption {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem !important;
  }

  .diagram-img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    background: #000;
    display: block;
  }

  .app-block {
    max-width: 400px;
  }

  .app-img {
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
</style>